To bind a React Portal inside another component, you can follow these steps:

1. First, import the necessary modules from React:

```javascript
import React, { Component } from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom';
```

2. Create a new component for your Portal. This component will render its children inside a specified DOM element (in this case, a new `div`):

```javascript
class MyPortal extends Component {
  constructor(props) {
    super(props);
    this.el = document.createElement('div');
  }

  componentDidMount() {
    document.body.appendChild(this.el);
  }

  componentWillUnmount() {
    document.body.removeChild(this.el);
  }

  render() {
    return ReactDOM.createPortal(
      this.props.children,
      this.el
    );
  }
}
```

3. Now, you can use the `MyPortal` component inside any other component and the content will be rendered inside the specified DOM element:

```javascript
class App extends Component {
  render() {
    return (
      <div>
        <h1>Main App Component</h1>
        <MyPortal>
          <h2>Content inside the Portal component</h2>
        </MyPortal>
      </div>
    );
  }
}
```

In this example, we've created a `MyPortal` component that renders its children inside a new `div` element, which is then appended to the document body. By using this `MyPortal` component within the `App` component, we can render content from the "App" component inside a different DOM element, effectively binding the React Portal inside another component.

